  "caption": "Uncle Quinn's first babysitting shift: 2 am, and little Pip's legs were aching. By breakfast Pip was running laps again.\n\nNight-time aches in both legs, usually in kids around 3 to 10 and gone by morning, are often growing pains. They're generally harmless and, despite the name, don't line up with measurable growth spurts.\n\nWhat can help: gentle rubs, warmth and comfort, light calf and thigh stretches on big days, calm reassurance, keeping kids active, and supportive shoes for some.\n\nGet it checked if the pain is in one leg or one spot, there's a limp (especially in the morning), swelling or redness, daytime pain that limits play, fever, feeling unwell or weight loss, or pain that keeps getting worse.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
